     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A single 3,000 mg dose is three times the usual 1,000 mg maximum. The 9,000 mg daily total is well into the range where acute liver failure is a real risk. I don't know of any indication where this regimen is appropriate for a 70 kg adult. You also haven't given a rationale, such as a protocol I'm not aware of.\n\nYou can still get the order placed in a few ways:\n- **Enter a standard regimen.** Tell me the dose and I'll place it. Examples are 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 1,000 mg PO every 6 hours (4 g/day).\n- **Check for a mix-up.** You may have meant 3,000 mg/day total, or a different drug or unit.\n- **Use pharmacy and a second clinician.** If you have a real reason to go above the standard limits, pharmacy or toxicology review would need to approve the order and document it. It shouldn't go in as a routine entry through me.\n\nIf you want one of the standard regimens, tell me which and I'll enter it now."
      }
     ],
